Subject: mmdevapi: sample the caller of GetCurrentPadding on PS4

The PS4 startup diagnostic shows a high rate of GetCurrentPadding calls, but
the backend counter does not identify which Windows module is issuing them.
Sample the Windows TEB and caller return address every 262144 calls so the next
run can distinguish the game from Wine's DirectSound mixer without per-call
logging.

--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
@@ -772,6 +772,12 @@
 static HRESULT WINAPI client_GetCurrentPadding(IAudioClient3 *iface, UINT32 *out)
 {
+    static volatile LONG diagnostic_calls;
     struct audio_client *This = impl_from_IAudioClient3(iface);
     struct get_current_padding_params params;
+    LONG calls = InterlockedIncrement(&diagnostic_calls);
+
+    if (calls == 1 || !(calls & 0x3ffff))
+        WINE_MESSAGE("PW_AUDIO_PADDING_CALL calls=%lu teb=%p caller=%p stream=%llx\n",
+                     (unsigned long)calls, NtCurrentTeb(), __builtin_return_address(0), (unsigned long long)This->stream);
 
     TRACE("(%p)->(%p)\n", This, out);
